rem The Race
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=232
rem Find the chance that the second
rem player wins a race to Goal points,
rem when the first flips a coin for 1
rem point and the second chooses to flip
rem until T heads for 2^(T-1) points

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Goal integer = 100

rem F[j] is the chance that the second
rem player wins when the first is to
rem move, the first having i points and
rem the second j. H is the same with the
rem second to move. A coin flip gives
rem F = (H(i+1) + H(i)) / 2, and H(i)
rem holds F(i, j) itself when the second
rem misses, so each T has a closed form
rem F = (H(i+1) + p F(i, j+g)) / (1 + p)
rem for chance p = 2^-T and gain g. Take
rem the best T for every cell.
T = 1 to 8 array
P = 0.5 ** T
G = 2 ** (T - 1)
Won = array shape 128 fill 1.0
Zero = array shape Goal fill 0.0
Hn = array shape Goal fill 0.0
F = array shape Goal fill 0.0
for I in (Goal - 1) to 0 by -1
  Row = concat Zero Won copy
  for J in (Goal - 1) to 0 by -1
    A = Row (J + G)
    Nxt = Hn J
    Cand' = (Nxt + P * A) / (1 + P)
    Best = Cand max
    Row J = Best
  end
  F = Row take Goal
  Hn = 2 * F - Hn
end
Answer = F 0 8 round
Answer print
